ITSM Platform Architecture (SaaS & On-Prem)

+-----------------------------------------------+
|                CLIENT USER                     |
|                                               |
|  (Browser)                                    |
|    |                                          |
|    v                                          |
|  +-------------------+                         |
|  |   React Frontend   |                         |
|  |  (SPA, NGINX)      |                         |
|  +-------------------+                         |
|          |                                      |
|          | REST/GraphQL API                      |
|          v                                      |
|  +------------------------+                     |
|  |    Backend API Server  | <--------------------+
|  | (Node.js/NestJS/etc.)  |                      |
|  +------------------------+                      |
|          |                                       |
|          | SQL / DB Queries                      |
|          v                                       |
|  +-------------------------+                     |
|  |      PostgreSQL DB      | <---+                |
|  | (Single or Multi-Tenant)|     |                |
|  +-------------------------+     |                |
|                                  |                |
|                                  |                |
|          Authentication          |                |
|          via OIDC / OAuth2       |                |
|                                  |                |
|          +--------------------+  |                |
|          |    Keycloak Auth    |  |                |
|          | (Auth Server, OIDC) |--+                |
|          +--------------------+                   |
|                                                   |
|---------------------------------------------------|
|                 DEPLOYMENT OPTIONS                 |
|---------------------------------------------------|
|                                                   |
|   1) SaaS Deployment:                              |
|      - Backend + Frontend + Keycloak + PostgreSQL |
|        run on Kubernetes cluster                   |
|      - Keycloak centralized auth for all tenants   |
|      - Multi-tenant DB or schema-based tenancy     |
|                                                   |
|   2) On-Prem Deployment (Client Side):            |
|      - Docker Compose stack:                        |
|         * React Frontend (NGINX container)         |
|         * Backend API container                      |
|         * Keycloak container + DB                    |
|         * PostgreSQL container                       |
|      - Separate isolated environment per customer   |
|      - Configurable via env files, no source code   |
|                                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------+


Packaging & Delivery Flow (On-Prem)


+------------------------------------------------------+
|  Package Delivered to Client:                         |
|  - Pre-built Docker images (frontend, backend, keycloak, postgres)   |
|  - Docker Compose YAML file                           |
|  - Config files (.env, config.json)                   |
|  - Installer script (optional)                        |
+------------------------------------------------------+

           |
           v

+------------------------------------------------------+
| Client runs:                                         |
|   docker-compose up -d                               |
|                                                      |
| Containers:                                          |
|   - Frontend (React + NGINX)                         |
|   - Backend API                                      |
|   - PostgreSQL DB                                    |
|   - Keycloak Auth Server + its DB                    |
+------------------------------------------------------+

           |
           v

+------------------------------------------------------+
| Client accesses ITSM platform via browser           |
| Authentication via Keycloak                          |
| Backend talks to PostgreSQL and Keycloak             |
+------------------------------------------------------+

Runtime Config & Security

+------------------------------+
|  Runtime Configuration        |
|  - .env for backend           |
|  - config.json fetched by FE  |
|  - Allows branding & env vars |
+------------------------------+

+------------------------------+
|  Security                    |
|  - HTTPS (SSL/TLS)           |
|  - JWT & OAuth2/OIDC         |
|  - RBAC in backend & Keycloak|
|  - Data encryption           |
|  - Audit logging             |
+------------------------------+


